{"kind":"deck","format":"deez.nut","version":2,"name":"MongoDB"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Document?","A BSON record that stores field-value pairs and is the basic unit of data in MongoDB."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Document?","Documents can contain nested documents and arrays, which often lets related data be stored together."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nDocuments can contain nested documents and arrays, which often lets related data be stored together.","Document"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Document}}: A BSON record that stores field-value pairs and is the basic unit of data in MongoDB.","Key fact: Documents can contain nested documents and arrays, which often lets related data be stored together."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Document","A BSON record that stores field-value pairs and is the basic unit of data in MongoDB."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Collection?","A grouping of MongoDB documents, roughly analogous to a table but without requiring every document to share the same shape."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Collection?","A collection is the main target for CRUD operations and indexes."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nA collection is the main target for CRUD operations and indexes.","Collection"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Collection}}: A grouping of MongoDB documents, roughly analogous to a table but without requiring every document to share the same shape.","Key fact: A collection is the main target for CRUD operations and indexes."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Collection","A grouping of MongoDB documents, roughly analogous to a table but without requiring every document to share the same shape."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Database?","A namespace that contains collections and related database-level metadata."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Database?","MongoDB deployments can host multiple databases, each with its own collections."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nMongoDB deployments can host multiple databases, each with its own collections.","Database"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Database}}: A namespace that contains collections and related database-level metadata.","Key fact: MongoDB deployments can host multiple databases, each with its own collections."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Database","A namespace that contains collections and related database-level metadata."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is BSON?","MongoDB's binary serialization format for documents, designed to support more data types than plain JSON."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about BSON?","BSON adds types such as dates, binary data, decimals, and ObjectIds while preserving a document model."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nBSON adds types such as dates, binary data, decimals, and ObjectIds while preserving a document model.","BSON"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::BSON}}: MongoDB's binary serialization format for documents, designed to support more data types than plain JSON.","Key fact: BSON adds types such as dates, binary data, decimals, and ObjectIds while preserving a document model."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["BSON","MongoDB's binary serialization format for documents, designed to support more data types than plain JSON."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is ObjectId?","A commonly used 12-byte BSON identifier type that MongoDB drivers can generate for the _id field."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about ObjectId?","ObjectIds are unique identifiers and contain a timestamp component, but applications should not treat them as perfectly ordered wall-clock values."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nObjectIds are unique identifiers and contain a timestamp component, but applications should not treat them as perfectly ordered wall-clock values.","ObjectId"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::ObjectId}}: A commonly used 12-byte BSON identifier type that MongoDB drivers can generate for the _id field.","Key fact: ObjectIds are unique identifiers and contain a timestamp component, but applications should not treat them as perfectly ordered wall-clock values."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["ObjectId","A commonly used 12-byte BSON identifier type that MongoDB drivers can generate for the _id field."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is _id field?","The field that uniquely identifies a document within a collection."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about _id field?","Every document in a standard collection must have a unique _id value, and MongoDB creates a unique index on it by default."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nEvery document in a standard collection must have a unique _id value, and MongoDB creates a unique index on it by default.","_id field"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::_id field}}: The field that uniquely identifies a document within a collection.","Key fact: Every document in a standard collection must have a unique _id value, and MongoDB creates a unique index on it by default."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["_id field","The field that uniquely identifies a document within a collection."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"fundamentals\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Embedded document?","A document stored as the value of a field inside another document."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Embedded document?","Embedding is useful when related data is usually read and updated together."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nEmbedding is useful when related data is usually read and updated together.","Embedded document"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Embedded document}}: A document stored as the value of a field inside another document.","Key fact: Embedding is useful when related data is usually read and updated together."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Embedded document","A document stored as the value of a field inside another document."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Array field?","A field whose value is an ordered BSON array."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Array field?","Arrays can hold scalar values or nested documents and can be queried with array-specific operators."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nArrays can hold scalar values or nested documents and can be queried with array-specific operators.","Array field"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Array field}}: A field whose value is an ordered BSON array.","Key fact: Arrays can hold scalar values or nested documents and can be queried with array-specific operators."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Array field","A field whose value is an ordered BSON array."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Dot notation?","The syntax used to address fields inside embedded documents and arrays, such as address.city."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"queries\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Dot notation?","Dot notation lets queries, projections, and updates target nested paths."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"queries\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nDot notation lets queries, projections, and updates target nested paths.","Dot notation"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"queries\"]"}
