{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Schema flexibility?","MongoDB's ability to store documents with different fields or shapes in the same collection."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Schema flexibility?","Flexible schema helps evolving applications, but deliberate schema design is still important for performance and correctness."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nFlexible schema helps evolving applications, but deliberate schema design is still important for performance and correctness.","Schema flexibility"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Schema flexibility}}: MongoDB's ability to store documents with different fields or shapes in the same collection.","Key fact: Flexible schema helps evolving applications, but deliberate schema design is still important for performance and correctness."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Schema flexibility","MongoDB's ability to store documents with different fields or shapes in the same collection."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Schema validation?","Rules attached to a collection that validate document structure or values when writes occur."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Schema validation?","Validation can enforce expectations without abandoning MongoDB's flexible document model."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nValidation can enforce expectations without abandoning MongoDB's flexible document model.","Schema validation"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"data-modeling\"]"}
