{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Single-field index?","An index whose key pattern contains one document field."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Single-field index?","Single-field indexes speed filters and sorts that align with that field and its ordering."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nSingle-field indexes speed filters and sorts that align with that field and its ordering.","Single-field index"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Single-field index}}: An index whose key pattern contains one document field.","Key fact: Single-field indexes speed filters and sorts that align with that field and its ordering."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Compound index?","An index whose key pattern contains multiple fields in a defined order."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Compound index?","Field order matters because compound indexes efficiently support queries that use appropriate prefixes of the key pattern."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nField order matters because compound indexes efficiently support queries that use appropriate prefixes of the key pattern.","Compound index"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Compound index}}: An index whose key pattern contains multiple fields in a defined order.","Key fact: Field order matters because compound indexes efficiently support queries that use appropriate prefixes of the key pattern."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Index prefix?","The leading field or fields of a compound index key pattern."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Index prefix?","A compound index can often support queries on its leading prefix even when later indexed fields are not used."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nA compound index can often support queries on its leading prefix even when later indexed fields are not used.","Index prefix"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Index prefix}}: The leading field or fields of a compound index key pattern.","Key fact: A compound index can often support queries on its leading prefix even when later indexed fields are not used."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Multikey index?","An index MongoDB creates when an indexed field contains array values."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Multikey index?","Multikey indexes let queries efficiently match array elements, with restrictions around indexing multiple array fields in a compound key."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nMultikey indexes let queries efficiently match array elements, with restrictions around indexing multiple array fields in a compound key.","Multikey index"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Multikey index}}: An index MongoDB creates when an indexed field contains array values.","Key fact: Multikey indexes let queries efficiently match array elements, with restrictions around indexing multiple array fields in a compound key."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Text index?","An index type that supports MongoDB text search on string content."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Text index?","Text indexes support token-oriented text search but are different from Atlas Search indexes and general regex matching."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nText indexes support token-oriented text search but are different from Atlas Search indexes and general regex matching.","Text index"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Text index}}: An index type that supports MongoDB text search on string content.","Key fact: Text indexes support token-oriented text search but are different from Atlas Search indexes and general regex matching."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Geospatial index?","An index used for location-aware queries such as proximity or geometric containment."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Geospatial index?","2dsphere indexes are used for spherical geometry and GeoJSON-style geospatial data."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\n2dsphere indexes are used for spherical geometry and GeoJSON-style geospatial data.","Geospatial index"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Geospatial index}}: An index used for location-aware queries such as proximity or geometric containment.","Key fact: 2dsphere indexes are used for spherical geometry and GeoJSON-style geospatial data."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Hashed index?","An index that stores hashes of indexed field values rather than preserving their natural order."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Hashed index?","Hashed indexes support equality distribution well and are used with hashed sharding, but they do not support range ordering on the original value."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nHashed indexes support equality distribution well and are used with hashed sharding, but they do not support range ordering on the original value.","Hashed index"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Hashed index}}: An index that stores hashes of indexed field values rather than preserving their natural order.","Key fact: Hashed indexes support equality distribution well and are used with hashed sharding, but they do not support range ordering on the original value."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Unique index?","An index that rejects documents whose indexed key would duplicate an existing indexed key."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Unique index?","Unique indexes enforce a data-integrity constraint as well as supporting indexed lookup."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nUnique indexes enforce a data-integrity constraint as well as supporting indexed lookup.","Unique index"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Unique index}}: An index that rejects documents whose indexed key would duplicate an existing indexed key.","Key fact: Unique indexes enforce a data-integrity constraint as well as supporting indexed lookup."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Sparse index?","An index that includes only documents where the indexed field exists."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Sparse index?","Sparse indexes omit documents missing the field, which changes both index contents and some query behaviors."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nSparse indexes omit documents missing the field, which changes both index contents and some query behaviors.","Sparse index"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Sparse index}}: An index that includes only documents where the indexed field exists.","Key fact: Sparse indexes omit documents missing the field, which changes both index contents and some query behaviors."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Partial index?","An index that contains only documents matching a specified filter expression."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Partial index?","Partial indexes can reduce index size and write overhead when only a subset of documents needs indexing."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nPartial indexes can reduce index size and write overhead when only a subset of documents needs indexing.","Partial index"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Partial index}}: An index that contains only documents matching a specified filter expression.","Key fact: Partial indexes can reduce index size and write overhead when only a subset of documents needs indexing."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is TTL index?","A special single-field index that allows MongoDB to automatically remove documents after a time condition is reached."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about TTL index?","TTL deletion is asynchronous, so applications should not depend on expiration happening at an exact instant."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nTTL deletion is asynchronous, so applications should not depend on expiration happening at an exact instant.","TTL index"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::TTL index}}: A special single-field index that allows MongoDB to automatically remove documents after a time condition is reached.","Key fact: TTL deletion is asynchronous, so applications should not depend on expiration happening at an exact instant."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Wildcard index?","An index that can index many or all fields beneath a path when field names are not known in advance."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Wildcard index?","Wildcard indexes help flexible-schema workloads but are not a substitute for carefully designed targeted indexes when query patterns are known."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nWildcard indexes help flexible-schema workloads but are not a substitute for carefully designed targeted indexes when query patterns are known.","Wildcard index"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Wildcard index}}: An index that can index many or all fields beneath a path when field names are not known in advance.","Key fact: Wildcard indexes help flexible-schema workloads but are not a substitute for carefully designed targeted indexes when query patterns are known."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Covered query?","A query MongoDB can answer entirely from an index without fetching the full documents."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Covered query?","Covered queries require the filter and returned fields to be satisfied by the index and can reduce document reads."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nCovered queries require the filter and returned fields to be satisfied by the index and can reduce document reads.","Covered query"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Covered query}}: A query MongoDB can answer entirely from an index without fetching the full documents.","Key fact: Covered queries require the filter and returned fields to be satisfied by the index and can reduce document reads."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Index selectivity?","How effectively an index predicate narrows the set of matching documents."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Index selectivity?","Highly selective predicates usually make indexes more valuable because fewer index entries and documents need examination."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nHighly selective predicates usually make indexes more valuable because fewer index entries and documents need examination.","Index selectivity"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Index selectivity}}: How effectively an index predicate narrows the set of matching documents.","Key fact: Highly selective predicates usually make indexes more valuable because fewer index entries and documents need examination."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is ESR guideline?","A compound-index ordering guideline that prioritizes Equality fields, then Sort fields, then Range fields for many query patterns."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about ESR guideline?","ESR is a guideline rather than a universal law; actual queries and explain plans should drive index design."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nESR is a guideline rather than a universal law; actual queries and explain plans should drive index design.","ESR guideline"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"indexes\"]"}
