{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is COLLSCAN?","An execution-plan stage indicating a collection scan."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"performance\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about COLLSCAN?","A COLLSCAN means MongoDB is scanning documents rather than using an index scan for that portion of the plan."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"performance\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nA COLLSCAN means MongoDB is scanning documents rather than using an index scan for that portion of the plan.","COLLSCAN"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"performance\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::COLLSCAN}}: An execution-plan stage indicating a collection scan.","Key fact: A COLLSCAN means MongoDB is scanning documents rather than using an index scan for that portion of the plan."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"performance\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is IXSCAN?","An execution-plan stage indicating an index scan."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"performance\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about IXSCAN?","IXSCAN shows that an index is being traversed, though the overall query can still require document fetches or additional work."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"performance\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nIXSCAN shows that an index is being traversed, though the overall query can still require document fetches or additional work.","IXSCAN"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"performance\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::IXSCAN}}: An execution-plan stage indicating an index scan.","Key fact: IXSCAN shows that an index is being traversed, though the overall query can still require document fetches or additional work."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"performance\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Replica set?","A group of mongod processes that maintain the same data set for redundancy and high availability."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Replica set?","Replica sets normally have one primary and one or more secondaries, with elections choosing a new primary after certain failures."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nReplica sets normally have one primary and one or more secondaries, with elections choosing a new primary after certain failures.","Replica set"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Replica set}}: A group of mongod processes that maintain the same data set for redundancy and high availability.","Key fact: Replica sets normally have one primary and one or more secondaries, with elections choosing a new primary after certain failures."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Primary?","The replica-set member that normally accepts writes."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Primary?","The primary records operations to the oplog so secondaries can replicate them."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nThe primary records operations to the oplog so secondaries can replicate them.","Primary"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Primary}}: The replica-set member that normally accepts writes.","Key fact: The primary records operations to the oplog so secondaries can replicate them."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Secondary?","A replica-set member that replicates the primary's oplog and maintains a copy of the data."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Secondary?","Secondaries can serve reads depending on read preference, but they do not normally accept application writes."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nSecondaries can serve reads depending on read preference, but they do not normally accept application writes.","Secondary"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Secondary}}: A replica-set member that replicates the primary's oplog and maintains a copy of the data.","Key fact: Secondaries can serve reads depending on read preference, but they do not normally accept application writes."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Election?","The process by which eligible replica-set members choose a primary."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Election?","Elections allow a replica set to recover write availability after the current primary becomes unavailable."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nElections allow a replica set to recover write availability after the current primary becomes unavailable.","Election"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Election}}: The process by which eligible replica-set members choose a primary.","Key fact: Elections allow a replica set to recover write availability after the current primary becomes unavailable."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Oplog?","The capped operations log used by replica-set members to replicate data-changing operations."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Oplog?","Secondaries continuously apply oplog entries to keep their data sets synchronized with the primary."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nSecondaries continuously apply oplog entries to keep their data sets synchronized with the primary.","Oplog"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Oplog}}: The capped operations log used by replica-set members to replicate data-changing operations.","Key fact: Secondaries continuously apply oplog entries to keep their data sets synchronized with the primary."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Read preference?","A setting that controls which replica-set members are eligible to serve a read."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Read preference?","Reading from secondaries can trade freshness or consistency characteristics for locality or read distribution."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nReading from secondaries can trade freshness or consistency characteristics for locality or read distribution.","Read preference"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Read preference}}: A setting that controls which replica-set members are eligible to serve a read.","Key fact: Reading from secondaries can trade freshness or consistency characteristics for locality or read distribution."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Read concern?","A setting that controls the consistency and isolation guarantees of data returned by read operations."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Read concern?","Read concern should be chosen together with write concern and application consistency requirements."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nRead concern should be chosen together with write concern and application consistency requirements.","Read concern"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Read concern}}: A setting that controls the consistency and isolation guarantees of data returned by read operations.","Key fact: Read concern should be chosen together with write concern and application consistency requirements."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Write concern?","A setting describing the acknowledgment level required before MongoDB reports a write as successful."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Write concern?","Stronger write concern can improve durability guarantees at the cost of additional latency."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nStronger write concern can improve durability guarantees at the cost of additional latency.","Write concern"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Write concern}}: A setting describing the acknowledgment level required before MongoDB reports a write as successful.","Key fact: Stronger write concern can improve durability guarantees at the cost of additional latency."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Majority write concern?","A write concern that requires acknowledgment based on a majority of voting data-bearing replica-set members."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Majority write concern?","Majority acknowledgment is commonly used when applications need writes to survive typical replica-set failovers."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nMajority acknowledgment is commonly used when applications need writes to survive typical replica-set failovers.","Majority write concern"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Majority write concern}}: A write concern that requires acknowledgment based on a majority of voting data-bearing replica-set members.","Key fact: Majority acknowledgment is commonly used when applications need writes to survive typical replica-set failovers."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Retryable writes?","Driver behavior that can automatically retry certain acknowledged write operations after transient network or primary errors."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Retryable writes?","Retryable writes improve resilience but applications still need idempotency awareness for operations outside supported retry semantics."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nRetryable writes improve resilience but applications still need idempotency awareness for operations outside supported retry semantics.","Retryable writes"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Retryable writes}}: Driver behavior that can automatically retry certain acknowledged write operations after transient network or primary errors.","Key fact: Retryable writes improve resilience but applications still need idempotency awareness for operations outside supported retry semantics."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"replication\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is Transaction?","A multi-operation unit that provides atomicity across supported operations and documents."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"transactions\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should you remember about Transaction?","Transactions are valuable when a data model truly requires multi-document atomicity, but good document modeling can often avoid needing them."],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"transactions\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Name the concept described by this key fact:\nTransactions are valuable when a data model truly requires multi-document atomicity, but good document modeling can often avoid needing them.","Transaction"],"tags_json":"[\"mongodb\",\"transactions\"]"}
